9. Build, test, and type-check results.
10. Performance measurements and testing conditions.
11. Deployment prerequisites.
12. Outstanding tasks requiring owner credentials, real configuration, editorial decisions, or external service access.

Assign each unresolved issue a severity:

- P0: release-blocking, such as critical security flaws, data corruption, or a fundamentally broken production build.
- P1: high-priority issue that materially affects safe launch, indexability, or core functionality.
- P2: important but non-blocking improvement.

For every important item, state whether it is verified, partially implemented, blocked, or not tested.

Provide exact commands and actual results for build and tests when the environment permits execution.

If a command fails, show the real failure and the corrective action taken or remaining.

Never fabricate test results, Search Console verification, Google indexing, AdSense approval, performance scores, or deployment status.

## 18. DEFINITION OF DONE

This phase is complete only when:

- The existing application builds successfully, or any remaining build blockers are explicitly identified.
- Core user-facing routes are tested.
- Public pages have appropriate SEO metadata and canonical behavior.
- Robots and sitemap endpoints return valid, consistent results.
- Published news articles follow a deliberate lifecycle and indexing policy.
- Private and administrative routes are appropriately protected and excluded from indexing.
- Structured data is valid and based on actual content.
- AdSense integration is configured honestly and does not violate the intended placement rules.
- Important security issues have been addressed or explicitly documented.
- Database persistence, background jobs, and provider failures are handled appropriately.
- Deployment instructions reflect the actual implementation.
- The final report distinguishes completed work from assumptions and external dependencies.

Begin by auditing the existing repository. Then implement the highest-priority fixes, run the available tests, verify the actual results, and deliver the final report.

Do not stop after generating a plan. Perform the work that can be completed within the available repository and runtime.
